452:{character:Narration}A-37 is sitting in front of a booth, dusting the barrel of a gun with a sponge attached to a wire.
453:A-37
454:  
455:{character:Ichihime}Mai, if you say yes, we will be able to organize a festival together, nyaa!
456:{character:Kana Fujita}Eh? That sounds suspicious. Could this be the aura of love that is absolutely forbidden to idols?
457:{character:Narration}This is troublesome. She must have gotten lost in the festival. I look around and see more visitors here than before. Perhaps it is because the performance is about to start, but the road is very busy with people walking everywhere.
458:{character:player}She is a lost child I ran into. Her parents didn't come even though we broadcasted her information.
459:{character:player}No wonder nobody came to us at the torii... Huh? Hold on, did you just say they had a fight?
460:{character:Narration}Moonlight streams in from the window, bathing the still figure of Mai and creating a solemn atmosphere.
461:{character:Mai Aihara}"Above the torii, the moon hides in the dark clouds... Under the torii, the girl grasps the lapel of a friend's jacket."
463:{character:Mai Aihara}Yes! The Temple of Moons and Mahjong Soul Shrine have a lot of shared history, and grandpa and everyone from the Mahjong Soul Shrine had known each other for a long time. Maybe he had mentioned something to them.
464:{character:Mai Aihara}"Noisy child, quieten down quickly. It is so noisy indeed."
465:{character:Mai Aihara}"Noisy child, rest in the arms of a loved one. It is so noisy indeed."
466:{character:Narration}Mai is surprised by my proposal, and her face turns red afterward.
467:{character:Mai Aihara}"Above the torii, the moon wears a conical hat... Under the torii, the girl grasps the Kagura bell tightly."
468:{character:Ichihime}After Mai's grandmother passed away, the old priest didn't organize a festival again because he was afraid of being reminded of her. Nyaa... how I miss the takoyaki sold at the festival of the Temple of Moons, nyaa.
469:{character:Narration}Just when the atmosphere became a little heavy, Kana, who is here to change shifts with us, appears in the nick of time. She is an artist under Osamu's company, and she has come to participate in idol events at the festival today.
470:{character:player}...Either way, I can't just leave a child here alone. What should I do?
471:{character:Narration}Mai seems to calm down after answering my question. She looks at the mother and daughter and slowly smiles.
472:{character:Mai Aihara}Actually, sometimes I think that my mom must have her own reasons, and that she must miss me at a certain moment somewhere... Maybe I can reconcile with my mom and untie the knot in my heart one day.
473:{character:Narration}The dance represents her efforts as a priestess, her determination to inherit the shrine from her grandfather, the loneliness she experienced in her childhood and her inner strength, and the recognition of her companions and herself. She sings...
474:{character:Sora Ichinose}No... But I read in a book that the larger the angular momentum of a circular object, the more stable it is... I haven't tried it myself though.
475:{character:Narration}With my encouragement, Mai decides to try out the game, and A-37 takes a few minutes to teach her how to hold a gun.
